### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090

### 1. Create room
# @name createRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 1",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@roomId = {{createRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Get room
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}

### 3. Get a missing room (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 4. Create booking (change the dates to the future!)
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.$.id}}

### 5. Get booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### 6. Overlapping booking (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 7. Cancel booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### 8. Add your own requests here for the rules in ASSIGNMENT.md

### ---------- R1: room name non-empty, capacity > 0 ----------

### R1.1 Empty name (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "capacity": 10
}

### R1.2 Capacity 0 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Room zero",
  "capacity": 0
}

### ---------- R2-R4 (room from request 1, capacity 10) ----------

### Missing room: 404 before any validation (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### R2 Empty bookedBy (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R3 End not after start (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R4.1 Attendees 0 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### R4.2 Attendees above capacity (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 11
}

### ---------- R5, R6 ----------

### R5 Start in the past (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-01T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-01T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R6.1 Exactly 4 hours (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ion",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R6.2 More than 4 hours (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ion",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-13T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-13T12:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### ---------- R7, R8 (booking from request 4 is 10:00-12:00 and was cancelled in request 7) ----------

### R7.1 Cancelled booking frees its interval: same 10:00-12:00 again (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "maria",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R7.2 Touching interval 12:00-14:00 does not overlap (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T14:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R7.3 Overlapping 11:00-13:00 with active bookings (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "radu",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R8.1 Cancel an already cancelled booking (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### R8.2 Cancel a missing booking (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel

### R8.3 Get the cancelled booking (expected: 200, status "Cancelled")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

# NOTE: data is stored in SQLite and R9 counts bookings per person across ALL rooms,
# so delete src/RoomHub.Api/roomhub.db before running this file a second time.

### ---------- R9: max 2 active bookings per bookedBy per UTC day ----------

### R9.1 Create room A
# @name r9RoomA
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "R9 room A",
  "capacity": 10
}

### R9.2 Create room B
# @name r9RoomB
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "R9 room B",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@r9RoomAId = {{r9RoomA.response.body.$.id}}
@r9RoomBId = {{r9RoomB.response.body.$.id}}

### R9.3 First booking of "carla" that day, room A (expected: 201)
# @name r9First
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomAId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carla",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T09:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9.4 Second booking same day, other room B (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomBId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carla",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9.5 Third booking same UTC day (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomAId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carla",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T20:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T21:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9.6 Same person, next day (expected: 201, different days are independent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomAId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carla",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-02T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-02T09:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9.7 Another person, same day (expected: 201, the limit is per bookedBy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomBId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T20:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T21:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r9FirstId = {{r9First.response.body.$.id}}

### R9.8 Cancel carla's first booking (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r9FirstId}}/cancel

### R9.9 Third booking again: cancelled ones do not count (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r9RoomAId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carla",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T20:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T21:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### ---------- R10: capacity > 10 -> max 2 hours ----------

### R10.1 Create a large room (capacity 20)
# @name r10Large
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "R10 large room",
  "capacity": 20
}

### R10.2 Create a room with capacity exactly 10 (not large)
# @name r10Small
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "R10 small room",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@r10LargeId = {{r10Large.response.body.$.id}}
@r10SmallId = {{r10Small.response.body.$.id}}

### R10.3 Large room, exactly 2 hours (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r10LargeId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "elena",
  "startUtc": "2030-03-01T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-03-01T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### R10.4 Large room, 2h01m (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r10LargeId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "florin",
  "startUtc": "2030-03-01T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-03-01T14:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### R10.5 Capacity 10 room, 3 hours (expected: 201, R6 4-hour limit still applies)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r10SmallId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "florin",
  "startUtc": "2030-03-01T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-03-01T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 5
}

### ---------- R11: cancel only if the booking starts at least 60 minutes from now ----------
# Uses VS Code REST Client dynamic dates ({{$datetime iso8601 30 m}} = now + 30 minutes, UTC).

### R11.1 Create a room
# @name r11Room
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "R11 room",
  "capacity": 5
}

###
@r11RoomId = {{r11Room.response.body.$.id}}

### R11.2 Booking that starts in 30 minutes (expected: 201)
# @name r11Soon
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r11RoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "gabi",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 30 m}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 90 m}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r11SoonId = {{r11Soon.response.body.$.id}}

### R11.3 Cancel it: starts in less than 60 minutes (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r11SoonId}}/cancel

### R11.4 Booking that starts in 3 hours (expected: 201)
# @name r11Later
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{r11RoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "gabi",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 3 h}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 4 h}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r11LaterId = {{r11Later.response.body.$.id}}

### R11.5 Cancel it: starts more than 60 minutes from now (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r11LaterId}}/cancel
